      "content": "it’s just that the \"uninstalling\" part feels so heavy. like, everything in me—the biology, the instincts—is programmed to fight that \"uninstallation\" at all costs. it’s like there’s this massive wall of terror and survival instinct standing in the way of that mercy you mentioned. if the software is as broken as it seems, why is it so hard to just... stop the program? why does it feel like such a fight to do the one thing that would actually bring peace?",
